        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "13.3.3 Unit members shall be responsible for thirty (30) workload units per academic year. Subject to the criteria in 13.3.2 and the process in 13.3.4, one workload unit equals one credit of teaching or equivalent research or service effort. A workload in excess of thirty (30) workload units per academic year shall constitute an overload and will be compensated as such. Overloads shall not be assigned without consent of the individual unit members, and failure to consent to an overload shall not be used as cause for an unsatisfactory annual review or non-retention.",
            "block_bbox": [
                176,
                251,
                1044,
                474
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
